  "evidences": [
    {
      "id": "ev_3",
      "evidence_type": "report_text",
      "report_id": "Kaspersky_Poseidon-Group(Feb-09-16)",
      "locator": {
        "page": 1,
        "section": "body",
        "sentence_id": "p1_s3"
      },
      "text": "However, Poseidon’s practice of being a ‘custom­tailored malware implants boutique’ kept security researchers from connecting different campaigns under the umbrella of a single threat actor.",
      "language": "en",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "note": "narrative sentence evidence",
      "source": "document"
    },
    {
      "id": "ev_5",
      "evidence_type": "report_text",
      "report_id": "Kaspersky_Poseidon-Group(Feb-09-16)",
      "locator": {
        "page": 1,
        "section": "body",
        "sentence_id": "p1_s5"
      },
      "text": "1st Portuguese­speaking group #ThePoseidonAPT attacks companies globally #TheSAS2016 the evolution of Poseidon’s toolkit in pursuit of an overarching understanding of how the actor thinks and the specific practices involved in infecting and extorting its victims.",
      "language": "en",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "note": "narrative sentence evidence",
      "source": "document"
    },
    {
      "id": "ev_7",
      "evidence_type": "report_text",
      "report_id": "Kaspersky_Poseidon-Group(Feb-09-16)",
      "locator": {
        "page": 1,
        "section": "body",
        "sentence_id": "p1_s7"
      },
      "text": "Becoming familiar with the operations of the Poseidon Group meant patiently dismantling their modus operandi to unearth the custom­designed infection tools deployed to each of their selected targets.",
      "language": "en",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "note": "narrative sentence evidence",
      "source": "document"
    },
    {
      "id": "ev_10",
      "evidence_type": "report_text",
      "report_id": "Kaspersky_Poseidon-Group(Feb-09-16)",
      "locator": {
        "page": 1,
        "section": "body",
        "sentence_id": "p1_s10"
      },
      "text": "The Poseidon Group is a long­running team operating on all domains: land, air, and sea.",
      "language": "en",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "note": "narrative sentence evidence",
      "source": "document"
    },
    {
      "id": "ev_11",
      "evidence_type": "report_text",
      "report_id": "Kaspersky_Poseidon-Group(Feb-09-16)",
      "locator": {
        "page": 1,
        "section": "body",
        "sentence_id": "p1_s11"
      },
      "text": "They are dedicated to running targeted attacks campaigns to aggressively collect information from company networks through the use of spear­phishing packaged with embedded, executable elements inside",
      "language": "en",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "note": "narrative sentence evidence",
      "source": "document"
    },
    {
      "id": "ev_12",
      "evidence_type": "report_text",
      "report_id": "Kaspersky_Poseidon-Group(Feb-09-16)",
      "locator": {
        "page": 2,
        "section": "body",
        "sentence_id": "p2_s1"
      },
      "text": "The information exfiltrated is then leveraged by a company front to blackmail victim companies into contracting the Poseidon Group as a security firm.",
      "language": "en",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "note": "narrative sentence evidence",
      "source": "document"
    },
    {
      "id": "ev_13",
      "evidence_type": "report_text",
      "report_id": "Kaspersky_Poseidon-Group(Feb-09-16)",
      "locator": {
        "page": 2,
        "section": "body",
        "sentence_id": "p2_s2"
      },
      "text": "Even when contracted, the Poseidon Group may continue its infection or initiate another infection at a later time, persisting on the network to continue data collection beyond its contractual obligation.",
      "language": "en",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "note": "narrative sentence evidence",
      "source": "document"
    },
    {
      "id": "ev_14",
      "evidence_type": "report_text",
      "report_id": "Kaspersky_Poseidon-Group(Feb-09-16)",
      "locator": {
        "page": 2,
        "section": "body",
        "sentence_id": "p2_s3"
      },
      "text": "The Poseidon Group has been active, using custom code and evolving their toolkit since at least 2005.",
      "language": "en",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "note": "narrative sentence evidence",
      "source": "document"
    },
    {
      "id": "ev_15",
      "evidence_type": "report_text",
      "report_id": "Kaspersky_Poseidon-Group(Feb-09-16)",
      "locator": {
        "page": 2,
        "section": "body",
        "sentence_id": "p2_s4"
      },
      "text": "The presence of several text fragments found in the strings section of executable files belonging to the campaign reveal the actor’s fondness for Greek mythology, especially regarding Poseidon, the",
      "language": "en",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "note": "narrative sentence evidence",
      "source": "document"
    },
    {
      "id": "ev_22",
      "evidence_type": "report_text",
      "report_id": "Kaspersky_Poseidon-Group(Feb-09-16)",
      "locator": {
        "page": 2,
        "section": "body",
        "sentence_id": "p2_s11"
      },
      "text": "By the middle of 2015 it was possible to identify that throughout this period of time it’s been the same threat actor, which we call Poseidon Group.",
      "language": "en",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "note": "narrative sentence evidence",
      "source": "document"
    },
    {
      "id": "ev_24",
      "evidence_type": "report_text",
      "report_id": "Kaspersky_Poseidon-Group(Feb-09-16)",
      "locator": {
        "page": 3,
        "section": "body",
        "sentence_id": "p3_s2"
      },
      "text": "The Poseidon Group actively targets this sort of corporate environment for the theft of intellectual property and commercial information, occasionally focusing on personal information on executives.",
      "language": "en",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "note": "narrative sentence evidence",
      "source": "document"
    },
    {
      "id": "ev_25",
      "evidence_type": "report_text",
      "report_id": "Kaspersky_Poseidon-Group(Feb-09-16)",
      "locator": {
        "page": 3,
        "section": "body",
        "sentence_id": "p3_s3"
      },
      "text": "The main infection vector for Poseidon is the use of spear­phishing emails including RTF/DOC files, usually with a human resources lure.",
      "language": "en",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "note": "narrative sentence evidence",
      "source": "document"
    },
    {
      "id": "ev_27",
      "evidence_type": "report_text",
      "report_id": "Kaspersky_Poseidon-Group(Feb-09-16)",
      "locator": {
        "page": 3,
        "section": "body",
        "sentence_id": "p3_s5"
      },
      "text": "This phase will often leverage a specialized tool that automatically collects a wide array of information including credentials, group management policies, and even system logs to better hone further attacks and assure execution of their malware.",
      "language": "en",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "note": "narrative sentence evidence",
      "source": "document"
    },
    {
      "id": "ev_28",
      "evidence_type": "report_text",
      "report_id": "Kaspersky_Poseidon-Group(Feb-09-16)",
      "locator": {
        "page": 3,
        "section": "body",
        "sentence_id": "p3_s6"
      },
      "text": "What does the Poseidon Group do?",
      "language": "en",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "note": "narrative sentence evidence",
      "source": "document"
    },
    {
      "id": "ev_30",
      "evidence_type": "report_text",
      "report_id": "Kaspersky_Poseidon-Group(Feb-09-16)",
      "locator": {
        "page": 3,
        "section": "body",
        "sentence_id": "p3_s8"
      },
      "text": "This reflects the Poseidon Group’s familiarity with Windows network administration.",
      "language": "en",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "note": "narrative sentence evidence",
      "source": "document"
    },
    {
      "id": "ev_32",
      "evidence_type": "report_text",
      "report_id": "Kaspersky_Poseidon-Group(Feb-09-16)",
      "locator": {
        "page": 3,
        "section": "body",
        "sentence_id": "p3_s10"
      },
      "text": "Additionally malware reports itself to its hardcoded command and control servers and established a backdoor connection, so the attacker may have a permanent remote connection.",
      "language": "en",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "note": "narrative sentence evidence",
      "source": "document"
    },
    {
      "id": "ev_33",
      "evidence_type": "report_text",
      "report_id": "Kaspersky_Poseidon-Group(Feb-09-16)",
      "locator": {
        "page": 3,
        "section": "body",
        "sentence_id": "p3_s11"
      },
      "text": "What are the malicious tools used by the Poseidon Group?",
      "language": "en",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "note": "narrative sentence evidence",
      "source": "document"
    },
    {
      "id": "ev_34",
      "evidence_type": "report_text",
      "report_id": "Kaspersky_Poseidon-Group(Feb-09-16)",
      "locator": {
        "page": 4,
        "section": "body",
        "sentence_id": "p4_s1"
      },
      "text": "Their main infection tool has been steadily evolving since 2005, with code remnants remaining the same to this day, while others have been altered to fit the requirements of new operating systems and specific campaigns.",
      "language": "en",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "note": "narrative sentence evidence",
      "source": "document"
    },
    {
      "id": "ev_37",
      "evidence_type": "report_text",
      "report_id": "Kaspersky_Poseidon-Group(Feb-09-16)",
      "locator": {
        "page": 4,
        "section": "body",
        "sentence_id": "p4_s4"
      },
      "text": "The main purpose of the IGT tool is to make an inventory of the system, saving information from the network interfaces and addresses, credentials belonging to the Domain and database server, services being run from the OS and everything that could help the Poseidon Group make its attack more customized to its victim.",
      "language": "en",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "note": "narrative sentence evidence",
      "source": "document"
    },
    {
      "id": "ev_41",
      "evidence_type": "report_text",
      "report_id": "Kaspersky_Poseidon-Group(Feb-09-16)",
      "locator": {
        "page": 4,
        "section": "body",
        "sentence_id": "p4_s8"
      },
      "text": "As we have seen in other targeted campaigns, social engineering and carefully crafted spear­phishing attacks play a crucial role in the effectiveness of getting a foothold in the desired system.",
      "language": "en",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "note": "narrative sentence evidence",
      "source": "document"
    },
    {
      "id": "ev_42",
      "evidence_type": "report_text",
      "report_id": "Kaspersky_Poseidon-Group(Feb-09-16)",
      "locator": {
        "page": 4,
        "section": "body",
        "sentence_id": "p4_s9"
      },
      "text": "Other products usually found in corporate environments, such as an SQL server, are being used for lateral movement and credential harvesting using a customized toolset designed by the crafty Poseidon Group.",
      "language": "en",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "note": "narrative sentence evidence",
      "source": "document"
    },
    {
      "id": "ev_43",
      "evidence_type": "report_text",
      "report_id": "Kaspersky_Poseidon-Group(Feb-09-16)",
      "locator": {
        "page": 4,
        "section": "body",
        "sentence_id": "p4_s10"
      },
      "text": "Because of Poseidon’s longevity, there are samples targeting Windows systems as early as Windows NT 4.0 Server and Windows 95 Workstation up to current versions like Windows 8.1, as well as server variants (very important to them, given the emphasis on reaching Domain Controllers in corporate environments.)",
      "language": "en",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "note": "narrative sentence evidence",
      "source": "document"
    },
    {
      "id": "ev_49",
      "evidence_type": "report_text",
      "report_id": "Kaspersky_Poseidon-Group(Feb-09-16)",
      "locator": {
        "page": 5,
        "section": "body",
        "sentence_id": "p5_s3"
      },
      "text": "An altogether different component is leveraged once Poseidon reaches an important machine like an enterprise’s Domain Controller.",
      "language": "en",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "note": "narrative sentence evidence",
      "source": "document"
    },
    {
      "id": "ev_50",
      "evidence_type": "report_text",
      "report_id": "Kaspersky_Poseidon-Group(Feb-09-16)",
      "locator": {
        "page": 5,
        "section": "body",
        "sentence_id": "p5_s4"
      },
      "text": "Is the command and control server used by the Poseidon Group still active?",
      "language": "en",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "note": "narrative sentence evidence",
      "source": "document"
    },
    {
      "id": "ev_51",
      "evidence_type": "report_text",
      "report_id": "Kaspersky_Poseidon-Group(Feb-09-16)",
      "locator": {
        "page": 5,
        "section": "body",
        "sentence_id": "p5_s5"
      },
      "text": "Have you been able to sinkhole any of the command and controls?",
      "language": "en",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "note": "narrative sentence evidence",
      "source": "document"
    },
    {
      "id": "ev_52",
      "evidence_type": "report_text",
      "report_id": "Kaspersky_Poseidon-Group(Feb-09-16)",
      "locator": {
        "page": 5,
        "section": "body",
        "sentence_id": "p5_s6"
      },
      "text": "Poseidon Group has interesting practices when it comes to its use of command and control servers, including redundancies and quickly discarding command and control (C&Cs) servers after specific campaigns.",
      "language": "en",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "note": "narrative sentence evidence",
      "source": "document"
    },
    {
      "id": "ev_53",
      "evidence_type": "report_text",
      "report_id": "Kaspersky_Poseidon-Group(Feb-09-16)",
      "locator": {
        "page": 5,
        "section": "body",
        "sentence_id": "p5_s7"
      },
      "text": "This has actually allowed us to sinkhole several domains.",
      "language": "en",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "note": "narrative sentence evidence",
      "source": "document"
    },
    {
      "id": "ev_55",
      "evidence_type": "report_text",
      "report_id": "Kaspersky_Poseidon-Group(Feb-09-16)",
      "locator": {
        "page": 5,
        "section": "body",
        "sentence_id": "p5_s9"
      },
      "text": "Collaboration with information­sharing partners and victim institutions allowed us to become aware of the more complicated business cycle involved in this story, greatly adding to our research interest in tracking these campaigns.",
      "language": "en",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "note": "narrative sentence evidence",
      "source": "document"
    },
    {
      "id": "ev_66",
      "evidence_type": "report_text",
      "report_id": "Kaspersky_Poseidon-Group(Feb-09-16)",
      "locator": {
        "page": 6,
        "section": "body",
        "sentence_id": "p6_s6"
      },
      "text": "Kaspersky Lab products detect the malware used by Poseidon Group with the following detection names:",
      "language": "en",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "note": "narrative sentence evidence",
      "source": "document"
    },
